= Choosing our enemies

In our media and campaign materials, who should we consider as our main opponents?

[? if enemies != 0 : Previously, we had considered the [+ enemies +] as our prior enemies. Is a change of direction necessary? ?]

- @anti_dem: The anti-democratic parties of the far right and left - the KPD, NSDAP, and DNVP.
- @far_right: The far right - the NSDAP and DNVP.
- @nsdap: The NSDAP alone.
- @kpd: The KPD.
- @bourgeois: The bourgeois parties - the Center, and DVP.
- @easy_discard

@social_fascists
on-arrival: enemies = "social facsists"; thalmannites_strength += 5; labor_wing_dissent += 5; conciliators_dissent += 5; workers_spd -= 4; spd_relation -= 10

Attacking the SPD and framing them as social fascists is popular among the Thalmannites and those who feel betrayed by the SPD. This will also hamper our ability to reconcile with the SPD in the future, angering the Conciliators and Labor Wing.

@far_right
on-arrival: enemies = "far right"; conciliators_strength += 5; conciliators_dissent -= 5; workers_nsdap -= 3; workers_dnvp -= 3;

Attacking the far right is popular among the entire party, although the Thalmannites considers the SPD parties to be just as dangerous.

@nsdap
on-arrival: enemies = "NSDAP"; labor_wing_strength += 5; ultras_strength += 5; nazi_urgency += 1; workers_nsdap -= 4;

[? if nazi_urgency == 0 or nsdap_r < 10 : The NSDAP is a tiny party right now, with more bark than bite. Many in our party are questioning our choices. ?][? if nazi_urgency > 0 and nsdap_r >= 10 : The Nazis are the most urgent problem for us to deal with, althought Thalmannites prefer we continue attacking the SPD. ?]

@bourgeois
on-arrival: enemies = "bourgeois parties"; thalmannite_strength += 8; thalmannite_dissent -= 5; dvp_relation -= 5; z_relation -= 5; labor_wing_dissent +=8; workers_z -= 3; workers_dvp -=3 coalition_dissent += 1

Our anti-bourgeois rhetoric is popular among most of the party, but may make it harder to build the Popular Front theorized by the Labor Wing.
